            <chunk name="Object" index="63">
              <items count="2">
                <item name="GUID" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">c9b2d725-6f87-4b07-af90-bd9aefef68eb</item>
                <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Tekton Summary</item>
              </items>
              <chunks count="1">
                <chunk name="Container">
                  <items count="15">
                    <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">The analysis summary as a readable report: maximum and mean displacement with the node they sit on, support reactions with an equilibrium check against the applied loads, extreme section forces with their location, and utilisation per EC5 computed here in the neutral layer - so it also works with the OpenSees backend, offline, without a licence or a design add-on. Every design number names the k_mod, gamma_M and service class it used. Buckling and lateral-torsional buckling are NOT verified: the neutral model carries no buckling length, and the report says so - a member that passes here may still fail on stability. Outputs the text, a CSV with one row per member, and the headline numbers separately; give 'path' a file name to write both to disk.</item>
                    <item name="GraftStandardOutputLines" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">true</item>
                    <item name="IconOverride" type_name="gh_drawing_bitmap" type_code="37">
                      <bitmap length="626"></bitmap>
                    </item>
                    <item name="InstanceGuid" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">695e48fc-fc75-4de1-8f12-06ac7de29bcd</item>
                    <item name="MarshGuids" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">true</item>
                    <item name="MarshInputs" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">true</item>
                    <item name="MarshOutputs" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">true</item>
                    <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Tekton Summary</item>
                    <item name="NickName" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">TSummary</item>
